{
  "summary": "Fixes binary verification in `contrib/verify-binaries/verify.py` so only distinct, non-revoked signatures from trusted keys satisfy the minimum signature threshold. It extracts full primary and subkey fingerprints from GnuPG `VALIDSIG` status lines to match against `--trusted-keys` and deduplicate signers by primary key, and adds corresponding unit tests.",
  "problem": "`verify_shasums_signature` counted untrusted keys towards the required threshold via `num_trusted = len(good_trusted) + len(good_untrusted)` (and included untrusted expired signatures under `--allow-expired`). Additionally, `parse_gpg_result` inspected only short key IDs from `GOODSIG` lines rather than full 40-character fingerprints, counted revoked signatures, and failed to deduplicate multiple signatures made by the same primary key.",
  "evidence": [
    "The diff in `verify.py` corroborates the logic flaw: `num_trusted` was computed directly as `len(good_trusted) + len(good_untrusted)`, allowing any valid signatures in the local GPG keyring to satisfy `--min-good-sigs` without matching `--trusted-keys` or local GPG trust."
  ],
