    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Changes are confined to `contrib/verify-binaries/`.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Fixes a security flaw in `contrib/verify-binaries/verify.py` where signatures from untrusted keys in the user's GPG keyring were erroneously added to `num_trusted` and satisfied `--min-good-sigs`. It ensures only distinct, non-revoked signers matching `--trusted-keys` or local GPG trust count toward verification, parses full fingerprints from GnuPG `VALIDSIG` lines, and deduplicates multiple signatures sharing a primary key. Without this fix, release binary verification could falsely succeed on binaries signed by untrusted keys present in a user's keyring.",
